  "executive_summary": "The Docker environment hosting the ICS lab presents critical security risks due to multiple containers running as root with elevated capabilities, exposed ports serving ICS components, and images with unpatched critical vulnerabilities. The most dangerous attack paths involve exploiting the simulation container's Docker socket mount (allowing arbitrary container creation) and the router's CAP_NET_ADMIN/CAP_NET_RAW capabilities (enabling network manipulation). High-value assets like the PLC (plc) and HMI (HMI) are directly exposed through published ports (8080, 6081) and run on images with unpatched critical vulnerabilities in core libraries (perl, OpenSSL). Network segmentation between admin/ICS/DMZ networks is unverified, and several containers (EWS, kali, simulation) have default credentials or unsecured mounts. The assessment was limited by the inability to verify network policies and the actual usage of certain capabilities.",
  "overall_risk": "critical",
